From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:57:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 427/427] Transform: start at the centre of mass when the
 object's origin is off the part
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The dragger starts at the object's origin (its Placement). Parts built by scripts or imported
from STEP often keep their Placement at the document origin with the geometry elsewhere, so the
X/Y/Z arrows appeared far from the part (reported on fcad-made furniture: 90 of 104 parts).
If the origin is outside the part's bounding box (enlarged by 1 %), the dialog now starts in
"Center of mass / centroid" mode; parts whose origin is on or in them keep "Object origin".
Preference User parameter:BaseApp/History/Dragger/CentroidWhenOriginOutside (default true) turns it off.

Japanese: "Center of mass / centroid" is 重心 (was the repeated 質量の中心 / 質量中心); the
edit banner reads 「…」を編集しています (it said 作っています also when moving a part).
